  "headline": "Bisleri States Disputed Water Batch Removed After FSSAI Scrutiny",
  "seoTitle": "Bisleri Responds to FSSAI Unsafe Water Prosecution",
  "metaDescription": "Bisleri reports that the bottled water batch flagged by FSSAI has been removed from circulation, as authorities intensify nationwide safety checks.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Bisleri stated that the affected water batch from its Goa facility has been removed from the market.",
    "The company maintains that subsequent production samples have met food safety standards following retesting.",
    "Regulators have launched broader surveillance of packaged drinking water brands across India following the incident."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) initiated prosecution proceedings against Bisleri International following reports that a sample of packaged drinking water from a Goa facility was found to be unsafe. Bisleri has publicly responded to the action, clarifying that the scrutinized batch is no longer in circulation. The company further noted that its Goa facility continues to operate without suspension, asserting that retesting of later production batches showed bromate levels were within the permitted safety limits. In response to the findings, food safety authorities in Goa have increased surveillance measures on various packaged water brands. Furthermore, reports indicate that national regulatory efforts are being expanded to conduct broader testing across the packaged drinking water industry to ensure general compliance with food safety standards throughout the country.",
